      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
